<div class="ip-faq">
  <div class="ip-faq__hd">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin:0 auto;">Common questions about Camden window film</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item ip-faq__item--open">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Is window film legal in New Jersey? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Yes. New Jersey state law places no restrictions on residential or commercial architectural window film. You can install solar, privacy, decorative, security, or anti-graffiti film on any home or business without a permit. If your property is governed by a Camden HOA or falls within a historic district, your documents may include reflectivity guidelines — we carry non-reflective film options that meet most requirements and can assist with the approval process.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">How much does window film cost in Camden, NJ? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Pricing depends on film type, glass area, and site accessibility. As a general guide: solar control film runs $5–$9 per sq ft installed; privacy and decorative film runs $6–$10 per sq ft; security film starts at $7–$12 per sq ft; anti-graffiti film starts at $4–$6 per sq ft. Most Camden homeowners spend $400–$900 for a typical room. Commercial projects are quoted by scope. All quotes are free and include a written estimate.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">How long does window film installation take? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">A standard residential install — three to five windows — typically takes 3–6 hours. A full-home project runs 6–10 hours. Anti-graffiti and decorative films can often be completed in a single afternoon. Commercial installations are scoped per project. We work around your schedule and leave the space clean.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">What warranty comes with window film? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">All installations include a lifetime manufacturer warranty against peeling, bubbling, delamination, and color shift. Brands like 3M, LLumar, Vista, and Solar Gard back their products directly. The warranty is property-bound and transfers automatically if you sell your home or business — a genuine selling point for Camden real estate.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">How much heat does window film block in South Jersey summers? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">High-performance solar control films block up to 85% of solar heat gain — the primary driver of summer overheating in Camden and South Jersey. Summers here regularly reach the upper 80s to mid-90s&deg;F with high humidity. Window film reduces hot spots near glass, lowers peak indoor temperatures, and cuts air-conditioning load, often reducing cooling energy costs by 20–30%. The U.S. Department of Energy notes that windows account for 25–30% of a building's total heating and cooling energy loss.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Does window film block UV rays? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Yes. Most architectural window films block 99% or more of UV-A and UV-B radiation — even clear, low-reflectivity films. UV radiation is the leading cause of fading in hardwood floors, upholstery, artwork, and retail merchandise. It also contributes to skin damage with prolonged exposure near windows. UV-blocking film reduces fading by up to 60% compared to unprotected glass without significantly reducing visible light.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Can window film be removed later? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Yes. Window film is professionally removable at any time with no permanent damage to the glass surface. The removal process uses heat and a mild adhesive solvent, leaving no scratches, marks, or residue. Renters, property managers, and owners who want a non-permanent upgrade often choose window film for exactly this flexibility.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Does window film work in winter, or only in summer? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Both. Solar control film reduces heat gain in summer. Certain low-emissivity (low-e) films also retain interior heat in winter by reflecting radiant energy back into the room — the same principle behind double-pane Low-E glass. This dual-season benefit is valuable in Camden, where January temperatures regularly dip into the 20s&deg;F. Year-round performance can reduce total HVAC energy use by 5–15%.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">What is the difference between privacy film and solar control film? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Solar control film is designed to reduce heat gain and glare while maintaining a clear outward view — it works by filtering infrared energy. Privacy film — including frosted, whiteout, and one-way mirror film — is designed to obscure the view into a space, either all day (frosted) or from one direction during daylight (one-way/reflective). Many Camden clients combine both: solar film on main living areas for energy savings, and frosted film on bathrooms, conference rooms, or street-facing glass for privacy.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Do you install anti-graffiti film on Camden commercial properties? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Yes. Anti-graffiti film (also called sacrificial film) is a clear protective layer applied to exterior glass and smooth surfaces. When vandalism occurs, the damaged film is simply peeled off and replaced at a fraction of the cost of glass replacement. It is popular on Camden storefronts along Federal Street, Broadway, and the waterfront commercial corridor, where scratch and spray vandalism are recurring issues.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Will window film damage my windows or void their warranty? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">No — when professionally installed on standard single-pane, double-pane, or tempered glass. For sealed insulated glass units (IGUs), we select film types rated for that glass to prevent heat-stress buildup. Our installers verify the glass specification before recommending any product. Most major glass manufacturers do not void warranties when an IGU-rated film is correctly installed.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Is there a tax credit or rebate for window film in New Jersey? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Potentially yes. The federal Inflation Reduction Act Section 25C tax credit covers qualifying building-envelope improvements — which can include energy-efficient window treatments — up to $1,200 per year for eligible residential projects. New Jersey's Clean Energy Program also offers rebates for commercial building efficiency upgrades. We recommend consulting a tax professional to confirm eligibility based on film specification and property type.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-faq__item">
    <div class="ip-faq__q">Do you offer free consultations in Camden, NJ? <span class="ip-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
    <div class="ip-faq__a">Yes. We offer free, no-obligation consultations at your home or business anywhere in Camden and throughout Camden County. During the visit we assess window type, sun exposure, and your goals, then provide a detailed written estimate. No pressure, no charge.</div>
  </div>
</div>

